{"t": 1794118181.1064517, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "\u26a0\ufe0f This change introduced a production regression.\n\n**Sentry issue:** https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/ \u2014 `LEDGER-WORKER-9A` ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit (expected 1100, got 1099). First seen in release `ledger-worker@2026.11.3`, suspect commit `8c2f1d0` from this PR.\n\nReplacing Decimal rounding with `int()` truncates toward zero instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit, so conversions come out up to one minor unit short and reconciliation fails (2,201 events so far). Fixing `worker/rates.py` to round half-up again with Decimal.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
